 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Pick a flat spot away from trees, trees are the worst for wind. A good rule is the tent should be able to fit in one direction. Then put the tree between you and the wind. Most tents aren't very strong against the wind, it's one of the biggest risks. That's the one. Cut it off as close to the trunk as you can, and cut the other branches as well. Keep the fire away from the tent and the tree, and keep the tent away from the fire. A little distance is usually enough. That's the plan. Have you thought about a groundsheet?",
